      "message": "I think these `PAGE_SIZE` to `mm_pte_size(mm)` conversions don\u0027t change anything. `mm/madvise.c` opts into `\u003clinux/p3s_user_pages.h\u003e`, and `walk_pgd_range()` enters `P3S_CONTEXT_REMOTE_MM(walk-\u003emm)` for the whole walk (aosp/4312517). So in the walk callbacks, `PAGE_SIZE` already is `mm_pte_size(vma-\u003evm_mm)`.\n\nThat covers `max_nr` here, plus `tlb_change_page_size()` and the loop increment in `madvise_cold_or_pageout_pte_range()`. `madvise_free_pte_range()` keeps `PAGE_SIZE` on the same lines.\n\nWould it be OK to keep the upstream lines and drop the `mm` local? The `vma_is_p3s_4k()` early return can stay as it is.",
